Reading the machine's own answer:
- bootall=4 -> the jump executed (kernel-jump-to kentry image-handle).
- T, U, M, X, Z marks present (tfacts=1 uflags=1; the fixture-literal T/U
  clauses admitted this image's own facts), and B is the KERNEL's own entry
  answering on port 0xE9 (kernel-out-u8 233 66).
- exit=43 is the kernel's own out 0xf4,21 -> (21 << 1) | 1 = 43, not the
  loader's fallback 33.
- kgot == klen == 110,872 (whole file read), c0 == s0 == 1052672 (0x101000),
  c1 == s1 == 1081344 (0x108000) — segments placed at their own p_paddr.
